# spamfilter 2.2 (B2a): domains the rbl module never looks up in the URL/
# e-mail/Message-ID blocklists (SURBL, URIBL, SEM, rspamd's own
# RSPAMD_URIBL ...). rspamd's stock modules.d/rbl.conf already lists this
# path in url_whitelist; it is a plain "set" map: one domain per line, the
# exact request string (the registrable domain the rbl module queries).
#
# Only single-owner domains and ESP infrastructure belong here. NEVER add a
# multi-tenant platform (the site config's platform_domains): any shop on
# it could host phishing. Platforms are handled by the filter
# (TH_OWN_PLATFORM_URIBL, B2b).

# The owner's own domains are NOT listed here: they come from the local site
# config (config/site.yml: mail_domains + webshop_domains) and are added to
# the rendered copy at container start (deploy/aio/aio_render.py).

# Outlook/Exchange Online Message-ID right-hand side (not a real domain;
# SEM_URIBL lists it via the "mid" selector)
hxcore.ol

# ESP infrastructure (SEM_URIBL ":mid" and ":from_smtp" hits on Mailjet)
mailjet.com

# 2.7.6: Klaviyo's shared link, tracking and signing domains. SURBL's abuse
# list carries manage.kmail-lists.com, so every Klaviyo newsletter got
# ABUSE_SURBL +5 (a shop's account and licence mails were moved). The
# shops' own links are still looked up.
kmail-lists.com
klclick.com
klclick1.com
klclick2.com
klclick3.com
klaviyomail.com
# 2.8 (C1): the DKIM check asks for the exact signing domain
shared.klaviyomail.com
